WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:05.731
The next morning Raoul's servant handed him a mud-spattered envelope. Recognizing Christine's handwriting, Raoul suspected she'd flung

2
00:00:05.732 --> 00:00:14.654
the note from a carriage, hoping someone would find it and deliver it. He tore open

3
00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:21.513
the envelope and read: Meet me at the masked ball at the opera house tomorrow night. Stand

4
00:00:21.514 --> 00:00:28.267
by the door in the little room near the rotunda. Wear a white cloak and a mask.

5
00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:37.291
Don't mention this appointment to anyone, and above all, don't let yourself be recognized! Christine Raoul

6
00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:44.067
didn't know what to think of Christine. Was she a victim or a deceitful person? If she

7
00:00:44.068 --> 00:00:48.951
were a victim, what monster had carried her off and how? Raoul thought if he had more

8
00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:55.413
information, he might begin to understand her erratic behavior. "She lost interest in music after her

9
00:00:56.076 --> 00:01:06.329
father's death, and then the Angel of Music appeared," Raoul thought, his heart swelling with jealousy. "Now

10
00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:16.716
he's taking her for late-night drives through the park. What game is she playing? How long

11
00:01:16.717 --> 00:01:24.459
should I put up with her toying with my affections?" Raoul alternately pitied Christine and despised her,

12
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:33.444
but the next day he bought a white cloak and mask. He arrived at the opera house

13
00:01:33.445 --> 00:01:38.752
a few minutes before midnight. Fighting his way through a crowd of guests, he arrived at

14
00:01:38.753 --> 00:01:41.775
the designated meeting place. Someone in a black cloak and mask passed by and squeezed his fingers.

15
00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:49.963
"Is that you, Christine?" Raoul asked. She turned and raised a finger to her lips to silence

16
00:01:49.964 --> 00:01:54.062
him. Raoul followed Christine as she made her way through the crowd. Having found her again,

17
00:01:54.689 --> 00:02:04.185
he was afraid to lose her. Once more he was absolutely in love with her. From time to time, Christine turned back to make sure Raoul was still behind her. As they passed through

18
00:02:04.186 --> 00:02:11.526
one room, Raoul noticed a group of people gathered around a man in a gruesome disguise.

19
00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:16.091
With a skull for a head, he was dressed all in scarlet. He wore a large, feather-trimmed

20
00:02:16.092 --> 00:02:23.195
hat with a long, red velvet cloak that trailed along the floor. Embroidered in gold on the

21
00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:30.678
back were these words: "Don't touch me! I am Red Death!" "Don't touch you, eh?" one

22
00:02:30.679 --> 00:02:36.708
young man said, reaching out toward Red Death. A skeletal hand shot out of a red sleeve

23
00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:45.111
and violently seized the man's wrist. He yelped in pain and terror. At this moment Raoul passed

24
00:02:45.112 --> 00:02:55.090
directly in front of Red Death and recognized the skull from the shadowy figure at Perros-Guirec!

25
00:02:56.149 --> 00:03:02.717
Raoul wanted to attack the man, but Christine grabbed his hand and dragged him from the room.

26
00:03:02.718 --> 00:03:09.928
Raoul felt as if they were being pursued but did not turn around for fear of

27
00:03:09.929 --> 00:03:13.943
losing Christine. They went up two flights of stairs to a box in the theater. Christine closed

28
00:03:13.944 --> 00:03:22.346
the door behind them and warned Raoul to stay at the back of the box, where he

29
00:03:22.347 --> 00:03:33.497
couldn't be seen from the stage area. While Raoul removed his mask, Christine put her ear to the door and listened. Then she opened the door and looked up and down the deserted

30
00:03:33.498 --> 00:03:39.336
corridor. "He must have gone up higher." Suddenly she exclaimed, "He's coming down again!" Just before Christine

31
00:03:39.337 --> 00:03:46.330
closed the door, Raoul saw a red shoe and the hem of a cloak on the

32
00:03:46.331 --> 00:03:51.874
stairs. "This time he won't escape me!" Raoul said. "Who won't escape you?" "The evil genius in the graveyard at Perros-Guirec! Your friend, the Angel of Music! I will confront him and finally discover

33
00:03:52.993 --> 00:03:59.359
the man you love and the one who loves you!" Raoul tried to push past Christine,

34
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.780
but she blocked the door. "In the name of our love, Raoul, you shall not pass." Raoul

35
00:04:04.781 --> 00:04:14.010
stopped. She had never said before that she loved him—perhaps this was a ruse to allow Red

36
00:04:14.011 --> 00:04:23.026
Death to escape. "You lie while my only goal in life has been to marry you!"

37
00:04:23.027 --> 00:04:29.179
Raoul shouted. "Impossible! You know someone of your rank could never marry someone like me!" Christine took

38
00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:35.838
off her mask, and Raoul noticed her pale skin and the sad shadows under her eyes.

39
00:04:35.839 --> 00:04:45.686
"I'm giving up singing." "Oh, so he's taking you off the stage," Raoul said bitterly. "Well, then

40
00:04:46.454 --> 00:04:55.070
maybe we'll run into each other some evening in the park." "I can't see you there or

41
00:04:55.071 --> 00:05:03.946
anywhere. It's over between us, Raoul. I must leave now." Christine put on her mask, opened

42
00:05:03.947 --> 00:05:09.274
the door, and forbade him to follow her. Raoul waited a few minutes, and then disregarding her

43
00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:18.500
orders, he returned to the party, where he searched fruitlessly for Red Death. With a throbbing headache,

44
00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:25.601
he wandered through the backstage passages until he came to Christine's dressing room. Raoul knocked on

45
00:05:25.602 --> 00:05:31.890
the door, but no one answered, so he entered the empty room. Hearing footsteps in the passage,

46
00:05:31.891 --> 00:05:41.116
he slipped behind the curtain that divided the dressing room. Christine entered and sat at her dressing

47
00:05:41.117 --> 00:05:49.695
table. "Poor Erik!" She sighed, removing her mask and putting her head down. Raoul wondered who

48
00:05:50.059 --> 00:05:55.575
Erik was and why Christine was sighing over him. Christine lifted her head as the faint sound

49
00:05:55.576 --> 00:06:01.585
of singing came from behind the walls. The sound grew louder as the voice drew nearer until

50
00:06:01.586 --> 00:06:08.431
it was actually in the dressing room. "I'm here, Erik, and I'm ready." Christine stood and

51
00:06:08.432 --> 00:06:18.513
addressed the voice, which was singing the wedding night song from Romeo and Juliet. Never in his

52
00:06:18.514 --> 00:06:23.087
life had Raoul heard anything more glorious. The voice was sweet, soft, yet undoubtedly male. "No wonder

53
00:06:23.088 --> 00:06:32.604
Christine is under this man's spell," he thought. "He has a beautiful, hypnotic voice with the

54
00:06:32.605 --> 00:06:39.364
power to bring out the best in Christine's own voice. How can I compete with that?" The

55
00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:45.378
voice was singing more passionately now. Peeking from behind the curtain, Raoul saw Christine stretch out

56
00:06:45.889 --> 00:06:52.594
her arms as she'd done in the graveyard. Her whole face lit up with joy. Raoul thought

57
00:06:52.595 --> 00:07:03.147
his heart would break, but he managed to draw back the curtain. There was no one else

58
00:07:03.148 --> 00:07:08.628
in the room. Christine moved toward the back of the room, which was covered by a

59
00:07:08.629 --> 00:07:15.080
large mirror. She could see her reflection, but not Raoul's because he was standing directly behind her.

60
00:07:15.081 --> 00:07:21.427
The voice sang again. Christine walked toward her image in the mirror and touched the glass. Raoul

61
00:07:21.428 --> 00:07:30.644
reached out to embrace her but was suddenly flung backward as a cold blast of air

62
00:07:30.645 --> 00:07:36.858
hit him. Christine had disappeared! Raoul frantically pressed his palms to the mirror. "Where did she go?"

